MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The lag bolt assortment feels like a natural next choice because I have been buying fastening tools and hardware, and it supports heavier wood fastening beyond my existing machine screws and rivet nuts.",
    "The duct tape, wire connectors and magnetic hooks fit practical workshop repair and organization needs. They offer useful functions alongside the mounting tapes and tools I already use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The anatomy model has no connection to the repair and fabrication tasks reflected in my recent purchases; I have no medical teaching or anatomy study need.",
    "The replacement sprayers and pressure gauge require specific uses I have not shown. My old dropper bottles do not imply a need for bulk sprayer replacements, and owning measuring tools does not establish a low-pressure measurement job."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Broad workshop or industrial usefulness seems to count too heavily when an item still needs a specific task or compatible equipment to be useful to me.",
    "My repeated fastener purchases seem to be taken as a reason to offer more screws, although another pack in one exact size may overlap with what I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters before I choose accessories: the burr shank must fit my tool, and connectors need suitable electrical specifications. An appealing use alone does not settle the choice.",
    "I value additions that fill a practical gap in my supplies. A complementary assortment is more compelling now than a narrowly sized pack without a matching project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my workshop repair and fastening interests, but sometimes confuse broad relevance with a current, compatible need."
}
